  "provider_query": "PEP 703 page that proposes making the CPython GIL optional",
  "answer": "**Primary page:** [PEP 703 – Making the Global Interpreter Lock Optional in CPython](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)\n\n1. **[PEP 703 – Making the Global Interpreter Lock Optional in CPython](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)** — Official PEP (Sam Gross; sponsor Łukasz Langa). Status: Final (historical). Proposes a `--disable-gil` build so CPython can run without the GIL; default builds stay GIL-enabled; ABI tag includes `t`.\n\n2. **[PEP 703 acceptance (Steering Council)](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython-acceptance/37075)** — Acceptance post (24 Oct 2023): three-phase rollout (experimental → supported → possible default), term “free-threaded,” and a possible rollback.\n\n3. **[Discourse: PEP 703 discussion](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional/22606)** — Main discussion thread on the proposal (build flags, ABI, object header changes).\n\n4. **[GitHub PR #2955 (python/peps)](https://github.com/python/peps/pull/2955)** — PR that added the PEP text (merged Jan 2023).\n\n5. **[What is PEP 703? (pydevtools handbook)](https://pydevtools.com/handbook/explanation/what-is-pep-703.md)** — Short summary: no-GIL build, biased refcounting, separate `t` ABI, experimental in 3.13 and supported (not default) in 3.14 under PEP 779.\n\n6. **[PEP 779 – Criteria for supported status for free-threaded Python](https://peps.python.org/pep-0779/)** — Follow-on PEP defining Phase II criteria so free-threaded CPython can be officially supported.\n\n7. **[PEP 803 – “abi3t”: Stable ABI for Free-Threaded Builds](https://peps.python.org/pep-0803/)** — Related packaging/ABI work required by free-threaded builds from PEP 703.\n\n8. **[PEP 805 – Safe Parallel Python](https://peps.python.org/pep-0805/)** — Later proposal that builds on PEP 703 and discusses safety limits of optional-GIL parallelism.",
